/**
 * @mainpage DA2026 - Compiler Register Allocation
 *
 * @section overview Overview
 *
 * This project implements **graph-coloring-based register allocation** for compilers.
 * It takes variable live ranges as input, builds an interference graph where nodes
 * represent **Webs** (merged live ranges of the same variable), and assigns physical
 * registers via graph coloring.
 *
 * @section pipeline Pipeline
 *
 * 1. **Parsing** - Reads live ranges and register configuration from input files.
 * 2. **Web Building** - Merges overlapping live ranges of the same variable into Webs.
 * 3. **Interference Graph** - Constructs a graph where edges connect Webs with overlapping live ranges.
 * 4. **Register Allocation** - Colors the graph using one of four algorithms:
 *    - @ref Allocator::runBasicAllocation "Basic" - greedy simplification (remove nodes with degree < N)
 *    - @ref Allocator::runSpillingAllocation "Spilling" - spills high-degree nodes to memory when stuck
 *    - @ref Allocator::runSplittingAllocation "Splitting" - splits Webs to reduce interference
 *    - @ref Allocator::runFreeAllocation "Free" - custom heuristic favoring splitting, with DSATUR coloring
 * 5. **Output** - Writes allocation results and colored DOT graphs.
 *
 * @section classes Key Classes
 *
 * - @ref Application - Top-level driver (batch/interactive modes)
 * - @ref Parser - Input file parser (live ranges + register config)
 * - @ref InterferenceGraph - Interference graph of Webs
 * - @ref Allocator - Graph coloring allocator with 4 algorithms
 * - @ref Web - A live range node in the interference graph
 * - @ref LiveRange - Raw live range read from input
 * - @ref ConfigRegisters - Configuration (register count, algorithm, K parameter)
 *
 * @section usage Usage
 *
 * @code
 * # Batch mode
 * ./myProg -b ranges.txt registers.txt allocation.txt
 *
 * # Interactive mode (no arguments)
 * ./myProg
 * @endcode
 *
 * In interactive mode, all settings (algorithm, register count, K parameter)
 * are configured through the menu. The output file path is prompted at run time.
 *
 * @section files Input Files
 *
 * - **ranges.txt** - Variable live ranges (one variable per line)
 * - **registers.txt** - Configuration for batch mode (register count, algorithm, K parameter)
 *
 * @section output Output
 *
 * - **allocation.txt** - Final register assignments per Web
 * - **allocation.txt.gv** - Interference graph DOT file
 * - **allocation.txt_allocated.gv** - Colored graph showing register assignments
 */
